After splitting, only a few integrals are ever needed:
\(\int \frac{dx}{x - a} = \ln|x - a| + c\) and \(\int \frac{dx}{ax + b} = \frac{1}{a}\ln|ax + b| + c\);
\(\int \frac{dx}{(x - a)^n} = \frac{(x - a)^{1-n}}{1 - n} + c\) for \(n \ne 1\);
\(\int \frac{2x}{x^2 + a^2}\,dx = \ln(x^2 + a^2) + c\);
\(\int \frac{dx}{x^2 + a^2} = \frac{1}{a}\tan^{-1}\frac{x}{a} + c\).
To find the constants: put the roots of the linear factors (each root removes all but one term); when no root is left, compare the coefficients of the powers of \(x\).
